<!--Post: 6763--><!--Time: 1107999938-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6763"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Featherw<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Featherw<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 09, 2005 - 5:45 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Yeah...that is possible IMO Skiller. <BR> <BR>Or...maybe he has a specfic victim in mind as his next venture..and he needed an exact address.  But..if that is the case, why didn&#39;t he just consult a phone book.  UNLESS, the person whose address he needs is conveniently unlisted?   <BR> <BR>Just a wild thought. <BR> <BR>I just have to wonder how anyone would know exactly how to bust into University files, not need to download anything...what could it have been that they needed.  Obviously something short in terms enough to either be written down or memorized.  That would be what I would think.  Either that, or someone accidentally hacked it...by error.   <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
