<!--Post: 6941--><!--Time: 1108085461-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6941"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Featherw<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Featherw<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 10, 2005 - 5:31 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I wish I had an idea Skiller.  I don&#39;t live in Kansas. I keep thinking Kechi, KS.  <BR> <BR>I think there is a possible link to BTK and the WSU files myself.   <BR> <BR>Notice the particular serverst that were hacked were ones used by specific students of specific studies.. <BR> <BR>&#39;The servers contained data for students and faculty in the College of Education, clients of the Speech-Language-Hearing Clinic and international students.&#39; <BR> <BR>...Clients of the Speech-LANGUAGE-Hearing Clinic and INTERNATIONAL students... <BR> <BR>I have to wonder what kind of LANGUAGE files were there... <BR> <BR>Thanks...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
